From 17e210550359dee5e4545b6d1ef7b566583396d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fulgor Nymvale <fulgor@nym-skyforge>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:46:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ImsMedia: declare JNIImsMediaService.setTestMode

The native JNI registration table (libimsmediajni.cpp) registers
setTestMode, but this class never declared it - RegisterNatives fails
with NoSuchMethodError, and ImsMediaServiceJni_OnLoad's pending
exception aborted com.android.telephony.imsmedia at loadLibrary on the
first call that opened a media session. Declare the method the table
expects; the native side is a logging stub.

Assisted-by: ZCode:GLM-5.3-Flash
Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
---
 .../android/telephony/imsmedia/JNIImsMediaService.java | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/service/src/com/android/telephony/imsmedia/JNIImsMediaService.java b/service/src/com/android/telephony/imsmedia/JNIImsMediaService.java
index ee6eb9d..fd627d4 100644
--- a/service/src/com/android/telephony/imsmedia/JNIImsMediaService.java
+++ b/service/src/com/android/telephony/imsmedia/JNIImsMediaService.java
@@ -87,6 +87,16 @@ public class JNIImsMediaService {
      */
     public static native String generateSprop(byte[] videoConfig);
 
+    /**
+     * Sets the test mode of the native library. Not implemented in native
+     * (a logging stub), but the JNI registration table registers it, and
+     * RegisterNatives fails with NoSuchMethodError when the Java method is
+     * missing - which aborted the whole media service at loadLibrary.
+     *
+     * @param testMode the test mode to set
+     */
+    public static native void setTestMode(int testMode);
+
     /**
      * Passes the application's asset manager reference to native which will be used to access
      * pause images assets during video call multitasking scenarios.
-- 
